# Go files check out with LF on every platform.
#
# core.autocrlf=true is the Windows default, and it makes `gofmt -l` report
# every checked-out .go file as unformatted — so the owned format gate is red
# before anyone has edited anything. A gate that is always red is a gate
# nobody reads: that is how an unformatted test table survived eight pushes
# to main before CI was believed.
#
# The blobs in git are already LF. This only fixes what lands in the working
# copy, and gofmt itself only ever writes LF.
*.go text eol=lf

# Shell scripts must be LF to run at all, on the box and in CI.
*.sh text eol=lf
